 not include antigen staining that  requires antigen retrieval  is mixed compatible with antigen  retrieval  yes so you can use basically  all kind of fixed tissues so  fpe tissue which involves such an  antigen  a retrieval protocol and here the most  important thing is that  all the antibodies you want to use are  compatible  with the retrieval method you are using  so you are not obliged to use just one  if you can make sure and test whether  the antibodies you want to use  are compatible with this method you can  use it  so our antibody portfolio has been  tested on the retrieval method  using tech buffer ph9  and heat antigen retrieval so for this  protocol we can tell you which  antibodies from us  are working but that doesn't mean that  this is the only protocol you can use  so yes the mix technology and the maxima  instrument are compatible  with fixation methods needing  antigen retrieval  thank you now this next question says  what is the manual logistics  and loading or preparing 100 antibodies  for use  on the mixed platform to be utilized all  100  and the second part says can it store  the number of stock antibodies for later  staining workflows  so basically for this you would have to  prepare  a 96 um deep well plate which we are  using  for the as a reagent carrier  um so you will simply pipette these  antibodies into  those welds and that's basically it  but if you want to skip this step you  can also  purchase from us ready to use place  the rear screen plate and then you can  even skip this  process um or this process step and this  is then  really almost without any uh needed  preparation  so you have full flexibility generating  your own  plates or using our ready to use plates  but it's not  really complicated it's just pipetting  antibodies into  a 96 well plate  thank you we're receiving such great  questions from the audience now this  next one is a two-part question  how are the colors distinguished and how  reliable  are the acquisitions 